{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968567-gifts","id":968567,"title":"Gifts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-13T09:27:22-07:00","id":968567,"title":"Gifts","content":"Such gifts like Scent of the Oathbreaker, I've read the gift's description and system but, is it perceivable with prime 1 or leaves any sort of energy signature on the victim to be noticed?<br /> A good friend of mine who is experienced with WTA stuff told me it can't be traced but I still need to confirm it.<br /> Also I've noticed in M20 that prime 2 can change auras, does that mean aura can be perceived with prime 1 too or it's just mind 1 that can do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12133,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","user":"Leonardo","date":". 09-13-2016, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T11:08:02-07:00","id":968623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leonardo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968567-gifts#post968567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Such gifts like Scent of the Oathbreaker, I've read the gift's description and system but, is it perceivable with prime 1 or leaves any sort of energy signature on the victim to be noticed?<br /> A good friend of mine who is experienced with WTA stuff told me it can't be traced but I still need to confirm it.<br /> Also I've noticed in M20 that prime 2 can change auras, does that mean aura can be perceived with prime 1 too or it's just mind 1 that can do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gifts are Spirit Powers and are generally better perceived through Spirit rather than Prime. Some that bring energy across the Gauntlet or alter damage types might be good candidates for Primesight, but Scent of the Oathbreaker is probably only detectable with Spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T13:41:49-07:00","id":968712,"title":"","content":"It really depends on the Storyteller. M20 presents a list of suggestions for a ST to choose, but does not give any real guidance. You can either rule that the powers of the other supernaturals are completely separate and do not/cannot interact with true magick at all, stipulate some thematically appropriate Spheres to be necessary for countering specific powers (ie Spirit for Gifts, Mind for Dominate, etc), or some other rule that you find convenient and appropriate. <br /> <br /> I'd say that true magick is capable of anything, you just need to figure out which Spheres and how many successes are necessary. If you want to determine the effect of a Gift after the fact, you might only need Spirit 1 to detect that a gift had been used, but I'd say you need a bunch of successes to get any real info other than &quot;yup, it's a spirit power of some kind.&quot; Some kind of ritual to build up enough successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T19:48:44-07:00","id":971684,"title":"","content":"Gifts are magic, so, yeah, mages <i>CAN</i> detect their use. Spirit is the Sphere that would find it easiest to detect Gifts, at least in my own games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T20:04:32-07:00","id":971694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968567-gifts?p=971684#post971684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gifts are magic, so, yeah, mages <i>CAN</i> detect their use. Spirit is the Sphere that would find it easiest to detect Gifts, at least in my own games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Detect their use, sure. But he is trying to counter the gift's effect in advance. Obviously he could counter magic the use of the gift if he is aware of its use at the time. But again, he is trying to immunize himself to its use in advance without understanding how the gift functions. Since he doesn't understand it (in character) he can't really set up a counter effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T20:08:44-07:00","id":971697,"title":"","content":"Ah! My apologies! Well, Spirit could theoretically do an anti-Gift parma magica...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T08:04:46-07:00","id":972528,"title":"","content":"Well, to me not Garou gifts are necessarily spirit related at all. Sure most of them are taught by spirits but that doesn't mean that you need the spirit sphere to defend against mental gifts such as roll over or Staredown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T10:41:11-07:00","id":972597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968567-gifts?p=972528#post972528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, to me not Garou gifts are necessarily spirit related at all. Sure most of them are taught by spirits but that doesn't mean that you need the spirit sphere to defend against mental gifts such as roll over or Staredown.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit will defend against <i>any</i> Gift since they are <i>literally</i> Spirit Powers. Mind will certainly defend against Staredown, Matter against Jam Tech, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T22:53:34-07:00","id":972947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968567-gifts?p=972597#post972597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit will defend against <i>any</i> Gift since they are <i>literally</i> Spirit Powers. Mind will certainly defend against Staredown, Matter against Jam Tech, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to which source?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T07:26:29-07:00","id":973126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968567-gifts?p=972947#post972947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to which source?</div> </div> </div> </div>Garou are half-spirit. Their powers are granted (and occasionally revoked) by Spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onyx Path Productions, on W20151,</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were the Garou armed only with claw, fang, and Rage, they would have lost the war for Gaia long ago. The arsenal of the Mother\u2019s warriors is varied and miraculous. In accordance with sacred pacts made at the dawn of time, spirits grant mystical blessings and powers \u2014 known as Gifts \u2014 to worthy Garou who know how to ask, and to those who impress the spirits. These Gifts attune werewolves to the spiritual power flowing throughout the Tellurian, and allow them to express that power in much the same fashion as spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T11:06:03-07:00","id":973241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968567-gifts?p=972947#post972947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to which source?</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf Apocalypse Storyteller's Handbook (Revised) states as follows:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Countermagic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magi may use countermagic to defend themselves against Gifts or fetish powers that are directly targeted at them. This is usually a matter of Spirit, although you may choose to allow other Spheres ot cancel certain other effects, such as using Mind to counter the Gift: Roll Over. The Arete roll uses the opposing Garou's Rank + 3 as a difficulty number; each success counters one of the werewolf's successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","name":"Rotwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T11:45:09-07:00","id":973262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rotwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968567-gifts?p=973241#post973241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolf Apocalypse Storyteller's Handbook (Revised) states as follows:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So at a super low Dif. That seems fair.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I agree Spirit can counter Gifts, as well as other Spheres being used, depending on the nature of the effect. But making it that ridiculously easy seems...dumb?<br /> Since I'm away from my computer, can anyone let me know if that's the same as of M20?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T12:37:02-07:00","id":973300,"title":"","content":"Dicepool disparity.<br /> <br /> It would be not fair to let a mage roll 3 dice at high diff against a attribute+ability combo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T12:37:21-07:00","id":973301,"title":"","content":"It might seem easy but it's also worth the notice employing countermagic counts as a full action, restricting the mage to his Arete dice (as possibly the lowest dicepool, varying from 2-5) in case he also decided to split and take a secondary action in the turn, i.e the Garou also used a point of Rage to use a Gift and attack in the same turn, the mage would have to split 2-5 to counter Gift AND dodge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","name":"Rotwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T12:51:17-07:00","id":973311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rotwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/968567-gifts?p=973301#post973301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might seem easy but it's also worth the notice employing countermagic counts as a full action, restricting the mage to his Arete dice (as possibly the lowest dicepool, varying from 2-5) in case he also decided to split and take a secondary action in the turn, i.e the Garou also used a point of Rage to use a Gift and attack in the same turn, the mage would have to split 2-5 to counter Gift AND dodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason I thought there was a reflexive countermagic dice pool?<br /> Also, I was once told that in Mage Arete Dice pools were never split (this might be an edition thing, or just how the players I knew ran it). So that even if you split dice pools that turn, the contermagic dice pool was full/equal to Arete.<br /> <br /> But even still, a Garou has to be Rank 4 to have the same countermagic dif as any beginner Mage (with both at 7 then, as far as I know)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:17:49-07:00","id":973342,"title":"","content":"Well...<br /> <br /> Night-folk receive automatic countermagick dice based on their Wits + Occult dice to cancel out ANY spell that <i>directly</i> target them, difficulty is by default 6 (which already is lower than the difficulty a beginner (or master mage, it only becomes heigher when we talk of Arete 8+ archmasters) has to employ countermagick against other magi, the Night-Folk doesn't need to have a dot in the Sphere he is trying to cancel out [a mage being targeted by Mind Sphere, when he himself doesn't possess a dot in Mind Sphere cannot employ countermagick on the effect]. Night-folk's countermagick is innate, whereas magi need a full action to employ it, other supernatural beings do it automatically and reflexively. Most Gifts require only one success to active, meaning if a mage doesn't cancel out ALL the successes (remember, he's dedicating a dicepool of 2-5 dice) he'll still be affect by the Gift (and he still needs to have Spirit Sphere or a fitting Sphere to try, under the Storyteller's discretion). For magick, some spells require a certain number of successes else the assault fizzles completely, so if a spell required three successes to be woven, but after the Night-Folk's innate countermagick it was reduced to two, the entire effect is scrapped entirely.<br /> <br /> The only one case where you can both do an Arete roll and an Ability + Attribute roll at their respective full dicepools in a given turn (save for using Time 3' extra actions, which cannot be used to employ magick, only mental/physical actions; or the use of drugs) is when violence is being used as focus, as reads:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Violence as a Focus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weapons, force, or martial arts can provide a focus for mystic or technological Arts, as shown in the Focus and the Arts section of Chapter Ten. In this case, the weapon or activity provides the \u201cgun and trigger\u201d of the spell. The mage fires a gun, throws a punch, makes a dodge, or takes whatever action is necessary to employ the focus. To reflect this activity, the player makes two rolls: an Arete (or Enlightenment) roll to see if the magick succeeds, and an appropriate Attribute + Ability roll to see if the attack hits its target. If the magick is the attack and the attack provides the magick, then in game terms, this is a single action \u2013 the mage is firing a gun as the act that casts the Effect, and although there are two rolls, it counts as only one action.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","user":"Rotwood","date":". 09-20-2016, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12152-rotwood","name":"Rotwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}